rota lap 4626, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes. Its instruction is to read by swallowing: run the actual thing up close rather than reading the sentence about it. Its cardinal seat asks what the round changed and whether running it again would change more; its fixed seat asks whether each seam carries two small answers, the asker's and the answerer's. Taste is what found this lap's red -- the scan was run against a two-file pen rather than read.
think Cold roster pass opened detached: 254 guards, 250 green, 2 red, 2 gated, tree_moved=no, run_verdict=guard_red.
think Reds first, and the two reds were one root. shim_reason read late_say_rostered=1, a reading held at zero, and standing_equipment read red behind it for that one line. tools/g/gitlink_dependent_witness.rish bound its scan at line 64 and said it at line 88, below the first assert on that binding -- so the census it tells a reader to read reached a reader only on the runs that passed, which are the runs nobody needs it for. The say moved above the asserts; both guards GREEN again, and the peer's own bare-say reasoning is kept beside a second note naming this one.
think Then the lane. amphora_bounds_agree states four relations, and last lap widened the first out of a typed roster. Reading (2), the alias groups, is the mirror of that fault: its roster is declared in the instrument, so where the first could not GROW, this one cannot SHRINK.
think The mechanism is smaller than that sentence. The group loop summed const LINES across all member names into one FOUND, skipped any name the room did not declare, and compared the numbers it happened to collect. Its only floor, FOUND < 2, counts lines rather than names.
think So one member declared twice at one value reads declarations=2, signatures=1, status=agree, verdict=ok, exit 0 -- and the comparison is entirely reading (1)'s own subject read twice. Proven on metal in a two-file pen before a byte was written, then again against the landed plant: elder exit 0, repaired exit 1.
obs Membership and agreement are two questions, so they are two readings now: members, present, declarations and missing print before any comparison; a group no member of which stands under this root reads absent and is skipped; a missing member reads incomplete and fails while naming who is gone; fewer than two distinct names present reads thin rather than agree.
obs The elder thin branch is subsumed rather than kept beside the new one. It fired on one LINE and only under the living root, which is why no plant could ever prove it -- a refusal a pen cannot reach is a refusal proven in one direction.
obs tools/fixtures/amphora_bounds_plants/alias_disagree/b.rye gained its third member constant in the same commit. A plant that reds for two reasons proves neither cleanly, and that plant is planted for the divergence.
obs The living room reads membership=whole for both groups, so the widening lowers nothing today. That is the water cardinal seat's own question answered: run it again and nothing more moves.
